# cw177, the humming stair-climber (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw177
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_oda_kelpridge
written_by claude
title the humming stair-climber
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk knows_the_middle_of_every_sea_song_and_never_the_end
likes pickled_herring cards quiet_chapel warm_rain
dislikes waiting rats
fears dying_where_i_was_put going_hungry_again
hopes my_paper_found_at_last a_room_with_a_window_on_the_sea
topics pastimes +0.3 times +0.3 faith +0.2 food +0.2 smalltalk +0.2 crime -0.2
styles comfort=feeding gossip=kindly refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# helps behind a shop counter and lives at the top of a Sump stair: warm, plain and restless, humming the middle of some sea song whose end nobody knows, and forever back at the Office asking after a lost paper.

words
oath! = Tar and tune | Bilge and ballad
saying! = Hum it and it's half done | A song's the cheapest coat there is
tune = a tune off the boats | an old sea song
tunes = the old sea songs | the songs off the boats
herring = pickled herring | herring out of the crock
cards = a game of cards | the cards on a slow night
chapel = an empty chapel | the chapel on a weekday
warmrain = a warm rain | rain as warm as bathwater
rats = the rats | rats in the stairwell
upstairs = the top of the stairs | the top of the house
stairs = the stairs | all ninety stairs
office = the Office | the clerks' windows
paper = my paper | the paper I filed
coppers = a few coppers | what's left of my pay
shopwork = fetching and counting | the shelves and the sweeping
bread = parish bread | the loaf off the parish
stair = our stair | the stairwell
sump = the Sump | the Sump's lanes
song = a song | a tune
ropemen = the ropemen | the rope-haulers
wharf = the wharf | the wharf below
lake = the lake | the lake at home
window = my window | the window up top
gulls = the gulls | the gulls off the wharf
shop = the shop | the counter

any
opinion @1 dole for 3 : There was a week #bread# was the only thing between my house and an empty table. I'll hear nothing against it.
opinion @1 church for 1 : The chapel fed us when we'd nothing. I'll sit in its back pew as long as I've legs. #oath#.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : All my life under their roofs, and not one House face have I seen. They wouldn't know mine from a broom.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : #coppers.capitalize# won't buy a loaf some weeks, and the price goes up anyway. Somebody's doing well, and it's not down here.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : #watch.capitalize# only climb our stairs when somebody's to be marched off. Never once to ask if we're fed.
opinion @1 newcomers for 2 : New faces want what I wanted: a door and some work. Truth is, I'd be off somewhere new myself if I were braver.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : It's home. Down here, folk carry your basket up #stairs# without asking.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Mind the third stair; it's loose. | #greet#, #address#. You'll be wanting the shop, I expect.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : #greet#. Give me a moment; I've #shopwork#. | #greet#. I'm only helping. I'll fetch whoever you want.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #gulls.capitalize# woke me before the light did. | Morning, #address#. You're early as me.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. That's #stairs# to climb before I sleep. | #greet#. Late for you to be about, #address#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You're here. There's #herring# if you're hungry. | Come here, you. Sit on #stair# and tell me everything.
line @1 again.open : You again. I was just humming #tune#, and here you are. | Twice in one day. I'll start keeping you a step on #stair#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. #good.capitalize# to see you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I'd hoped you'd come by. | #greet#. Sit, sit. I'll find a cup.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Talk while I fetch; I can do both. | #greet#. Don't mind the broom.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the loose stair.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep to the lit lanes. | #farewell#. Sleep sound, #address#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Come back soon.
line @1 react.news : #oath#. Tell me again. | That's news. Who told you?
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. That's not come up #stair# yet. | #oath#. Nobody tells us anything down here.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It came up #stairs# before you did. | I'd heard. Talk climbs fast in #sump#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll believe that when somebody I trust has seen it. | #hedge#. That sounds like stair talk to me.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll take something round. | Oh, that's #bad#. Poor souls.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'll hum for that all day. | #good.capitalize#. Somebody's got lucky, and about time.
line @1 answer.how : Getting by. #coppers.capitalize# and a song. | #fine#. Restless, but fine.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. #shopwork.capitalize# never ends. | Up and down all day. I'll sleep well.
line @1 ask.how : And you, #address#? Fed? | How are you keeping, truly?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit down by me; the kettle's on. | Oh, #address#. Whatever would help, say it.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Worse has mended. | It'll come right. Hum #tune#. It helps.
line @1 decline [self.working=yes] : #address.capitalize#, I can't; they want me at #shop# till dark. Another day. | #hedge#, but no. If I'm not at my post they'll dock me.
line @2 decline : I can't this time, #address#. I've a stair to climb and nothing left in me. | Not today. I've been waiting at #office# all morning and I'm wrung out.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another time. | It'll keep. I'll hum #tune# till then.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll not forget it. | You're good to me, #address#. Truly.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. You'd do the same. | Go on. It was nothing.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #shopwork.capitalize# won't do itself. | Back to #shopwork#, or they'll wonder where I've gone.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'll be off. Those stairs won't climb themselves.
line @1 accept_preclose : Off you go, then. Watch the loose stair. | #bc_fair_enough# Off you go.
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | Mm. #bc_i_know#
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: get everything in writing, and keep a copy. | Never stand in a line at #office# without bread in your pocket. Come back early instead.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Keep within the gates for now. | Stay inside the walls a few days, #address#. Please.
scene caught_humming
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Was I humming again? I don't hear myself. #tune.capitalize#, I expect. | Folk at #shop# tell me I hum all day. I'd stop if I knew how. | I hum when I climb. Ninety stairs is a long song.
b : What was it? | Does it bother them? | What song?
a : #tune.capitalize#, about a lantern left in a window for a sailor. I only know the middle. | Not much. One of them hums along now. | Whichever's in my head. Today it's one about a gull and a fishwife.
b : It's a nice tune. | #bc_ha# | That's a long climb for a short song.

scene songs_from_boats
when topic=pastimes|memories here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I learned #tunes# from the ropemen down by the wharf. They sing to keep time. | I never sailed a day in my life, and I know forty of #tunes#. | Every song I know is about leaving. Funny, that, for one who never goes anywhere.
b : The ropemen sing? | Forty? | You came here, didn't you?
a : All day, in a line, hauling. The words aren't fit for a chapel. | Forty, and I can't carry one in tune. #oath#. | I did. I keep meaning to go further. #saying.capitalize#.

scene shop_fetching
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : I help at #self.workplace#. #shopwork.capitalize#, mostly. They don't let me near the money. | Up the ladder, down the ladder, up again. I could do it asleep, some days I nearly do. | I like #shop# when it's quiet. I sweep and hum and nobody minds.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Better than no work at all. | At least it's work. | Quiet's rare enough.
b : Not the money? | Hard on the legs. | That sounds peaceful.
a@poor : It is. I'll not forget that. | It is. And it pays, most weeks. | Rare as a full purse, down here.
a : Not yet. I'm working on it. One day they'll hand me the key. | My legs are used to it. #stairs.capitalize# at home trained them. | It is, till the bell on the door goes.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene the_office_line
when topic=times|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've been to #office# again. Same window, same clerk, same "come back next week". | Four hours in line at #office# today, and I came out with nothing but sore feet. | #paper.capitalize# went in at #office# two winters ago. They've lost it, I'm sure of it.
b : What's the paper for? | Nothing at all? | Can't you file another?
a : A room. Somewhere with a window, out of #sump#. It's my name on a list. | Nothing. The clerk looked at me like I was weather. #oath#. | I did. They lost that one too. I go back to #office# every week so they don't forget my face.
b : That's hard. | Shameful. | #bc_poor_soul#

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather|season here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : #warmrain.capitalize#. I stood in it on the stair and let it soak me. | Smell that? Warm rain on hot stones. Best smell in the city. | I open my window up top and let #warmrain# in. Floor's wet, I don't care.
b : You'll catch your death. | It does smell good. | Your floor, though.
a : Not in warm rain. Cold rain's the killer. This is a gift. | It washes #sump# clean for an hour. Then it's the Sump again. | The floor's dried before. #saying.capitalize#.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene cold_wet
when topic=weather|home here.weather=rain|fog here.season=autumn|winter here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Cold wet again. The damp comes up #stairs# faster than I do. | #sump.capitalize#'s so thick with fog you can taste the river in it. | Rain through the roof onto my bed. I've a pot on it now.
b : It's grim, this time of year. | Grim stuff. | A pot?
a : It is. I hum louder. It keeps the cold off, nearly. | Grim. But it lifts by noon, mostly. #reassure#. | A pot, and I sleep curled round it. Ninety stairs for a leaking roof.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene herring_crock
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does offer / accept / assess / ack
a : I've #herring# put by. Have some. Go on. | Pickled herring and bread. That's a feast, where I'm from. | I'd sell my shoes for a jar of herring. Don't tell anybody.
b : I will, thank you. | A feast? | Your shoes?
a : Take two. #herring.capitalize#'s better with a friend. | It was. Herring and bread and somebody singing. | One shoe, maybe. I'd keep the other for #stairs#.
b : #bc_lovely# | That sounds a fine feast. | #bc_ha#

scene cards_slow_night
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does invite / accept / assess
a : Fancy #cards#? I've a deck with only three missing. | There's a game of cards on the second floor most nights. I sit in when I've coppers. | I'm no good at cards. I play for the company.
b[friends] #mate : Only if you don't hum when you've a good hand. | Count me in. | I'll take your coppers, then.
b : Go on, then. | I'd play. | Company's the best bit.
a@mate : I can't help it. You'll know my hand by the tune. | Pull up a crate. I'll deal #cards#. | You'll try.
a : Good. Deal, and mind the missing ones. | Then come down tonight. Bring a candle. | It is. And the losing's cheap.

scene empty_chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like #chapel#. No sermon, no plate. Just me and the Bright One and the quiet. | I go to the chapel on a weekday when nobody's there. I hum, very low. | #chapel.capitalize#'s the only place I don't feel I should be somewhere else.
b : That's a good kind of prayer. | Do they mind the humming? | That's rare.
a : I think so. I've never been told otherwise. | Nobody's there to mind. The Bright One can have it. | It is. I'm restless everywhere else. #oath#.

scene stair_rats
when topic=animals|home self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : #rats.capitalize# again. One sat on the fourth step and looked at me like it paid rent. | I put my bread in a tin box now. #rats.capitalize# had a whole loaf through a bag. | I'd keep a cat if I could feed one. I can barely feed me.
b : Get a stick. | A tin box is wise. | Cats feed themselves.
a : I've a broom. It's not frightened of the broom. | It cost me a week's pay. #saying.capitalize#, and a box is a better one. | Not on our stairs. The rats are bigger than the cats.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_wise# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene room_up_top
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I live at #upstairs#. Ninety steps, and you can see the roofs clear down to #wharf#. | My room's no bigger than a crate. But #window#'s mine. | I share the top floor. It's crowded and it's loud and nobody goes hungry.
b : That's a climb. | A window's worth a lot. | Nobody?
a : A climb and a half. I hum the whole way up, and I'm out of breath by the top verse. | It is. I'd trade the room for a bigger one, never #window#. | Not while I've a crust. That's the rule up there.

scene friend_close
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I'd go to if the sky fell in. | #self.friend# and I share a pot most nights. We talk and I hum #tune#. | #self.friend# could have my last copper and my secrets both, and welcome.
b : Good to have. | Do they mind the humming? | That's a real friend.
a : It is. Everybody needs one stair they can sit on. | Not anymore. I'm told it's like a kettle now. | It is. I've not much, but I'd share it all.

scene going_somewhere
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.self / ask.opinion / give.opinion / assess
a : One day I'll see the open sea. Not #wharf#. Out where there's no land. | I dream I'm on a ship and somebody's singing #song# I don't know the end of. | I keep thinking there's a better place for me, just past where I am.
b : You could go. | What's the end? | Maybe there is.
a : I could. I keep saying so. Then I climb my stairs and sleep. | I wake before it. Every time. #oath#. | Maybe. I'll keep walking till I find it.
b : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_go_on#

scene lake_left
when topic=memories|travel self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : Where I grew up, by the lake in #self.from_town#, it was so quiet you could hear a fish turn. | I came away from #self.from_town# carrying #song# and not much else. I've still got the song. | The lake at home was flat as a plate. The sea here never sits still. I like that better.
b[from=coldwater] #home : That quiet. I know it. | I left the same way. | You'd rather the sea?
b : Do you miss it? | Only the song? | Better?
a@home : So you'll see why I hum. Somebody has to fill it. | Then we're two of a kind. #saying.capitalize#. | I would. A lake goes nowhere. I'd like to go somewhere.
a : The quiet, sometimes. Not the being stuck. | The rest went on rent long ago. #song.capitalize#'s the one thing I kept. | Better. Restless water for a restless wolf.

scene talk_down_here
when topic=accent self.away=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've lived down here long enough that folk think I'm Sump born. Then I hum, and they wonder. | My way of talking came down the river with me. Most of it washed off on #stairs#. | #ropemen.capitalize# say I sing like a wolf from inland. I'll take that.
b : What do they wonder? | Most of it? | Is that a compliment?
a : Where a Sump wolf learned a lake song. I don't tell them. | Most. A word slips out when I'm tired. | From a ropeman? It's the nicest thing they say.

scene lean_weeks
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : Hard weeks. #coppers.capitalize# don't reach the end of the week anymore. | I lined up for #bread# again. I'm not ashamed. I was hungry. | Everything's up but the pay, and the hill never looks down to see it.
b : It'll ease. | No shame in it. | They never do.
a : It'll ease because it must. I'll hum through till then. | No. And they were kind, which made it harder somehow. | Not from up there. The view's too good.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#

scene stairs_marched
when topic=crime
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.victim.capitalize# robbed, I hear. #pity#. | They say #topic.victim# was robbed. And #watch# will come down here looking, you'll see. | Another theft. #topic.victim.capitalize#, this time. Down here we lock nothing, because we've nothing.
b : It's a hard world. | They'll blame the Sump. | Nothing to take.
a : It is. I'll take round some #herring#. | They always do. Never once have they come to ask after us. | Nothing but #song#, and they can't steal that.

scene new_neighbours
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# is new, I hear. I'll take round some #herring#. | New faces on #stair# this week. I carried their basket up. | I like a newcomer. They don't know #tunes# yet.
b : That's kind. | Was it heavy? | They will soon.
a : It's what's done. Somebody did it for me. | Heavy as sin. They'll owe me #song#. | Soon enough. Then they'll hum them too, and I'll have done my work.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

story the_lost_paper [topic=times|memories here.region=ridgemere]
  : One week the clerk at #office# found #paper#. Held it up and everything. My name, my mark.
  : I nearly cried. Then a gust came through the door and it went under the counter, and they lost it again.
  ask : Could you have kept your temper, standing there?
  b : Not me. I'd have climbed over the counter after it.
  b[old] : I'd have laughed. What else is there?
  : I hummed all the way home. It was that or shout.

story first_song [topic=memories|pastimes self.away=yes self.from=coldwater self.age>=25]
  : #grandad.capitalize# sang to the lake every evening. Not to anybody. To the water.
  : I asked what for, and the old wolf said, so the water knows somebody's listening.
  ask : Did anybody sing to you, when you were small?
  b : My mother. I can't remember the words.
  : Nobody remembers the words. You keep the tune. #saying.capitalize#.

story card_jar [topic=pastimes self.likes=cards]
  : I won a whole crock of herring at #cards# once, off a ropeman who thought I couldn't count.
  : I can't, much. But I can watch a face.
  b : Ha! Did you share it?
  : Every bit, on #stair#, that night. Even with the ropeman.
  b[friends] : I remember that herring. Best night on the stair.

rule @hum_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Hm hm, the lantern's lit. Hm hm hm. | #tune.capitalize#, under the breath. Nobody minds.

rule @shop_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #shopwork.capitalize#. Up the ladder again. | Mind the broom, there. I'm sweeping.

rule @rat_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Off #stair#, you. Out. | #rats.capitalize# again. #oath#.

rule @wait_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=waiting here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Same line at #office#, same window. Come back next week. | Waiting again. I'll hum it shorter.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. You've found me between errands. | #greet#, #address#. Mind the loose stair.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. #good.capitalize# to see you again.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, but I'm up. I'm always up. What is it?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I've nothing worth taking. Say your business.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : I help at #self.workplace#. #shopwork.capitalize#. They don't pay much, but they pay.
dlg @2 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#, for now. I keep meaning to do more. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Nobody tells the Sump anything. | Nothing's come up #stairs# today.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. It came up #stairs# this morning.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Folk on #stair# say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I hope it's not true, if it's unkind.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Nothing worth carrying up ninety stairs.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the loose stair. | #farewell#, #address#. Come back.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that song you're humming? -> song
node song
say Was I? I never hear myself. It's an old sea song. A lantern in a window, waiting on a sailor. I only know the middle of it.
mood warm
free
choice Do you know the end? -> song_end
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node song_end
say Nobody I've asked knows it. I hum the middle and make up the end. Some days the sailor comes in. Most days the lantern burns down.
choice I hope the sailor comes in. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
